# Git authorship (strict)

Commits and pushes for this repo must appear as **DhanushPrince only**. Never Cursor Agent.

## Never

- Add `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` (or any `cursoragent@` / “Made with Cursor” trailer).
- Commit or push with author/committer set to Cursor Agent.
- Leave a Cursor co-author badge on GitHub after a commit the agent created.

## When committing

1. Author and committer must be **DhanushPrince** `<r.dhanush307@gmail.com>` (repo local `user.name` / `user.email`).
2. After any `git commit` created in-agent, **verify** before push:
   ```bash
   git log -1 --format='%B'
   ```
   If a Cursor trailer is present, strip it **before** push (do not push the trailed commit):
   ```bash
   # Prefer commit-tree rewrite so Cursor cannot re-inject the trailer:
   TREE=$(git rev-parse HEAD^{tree})
   PARENT=$(git rev-parse HEAD^)
   NEW=$(printf '%s\n' "$(git log -1 --format=%s)" | \
     GIT_AUTHOR_NAME='DhanushPrince' GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL='r.dhanush307@gmail.com' \
     GIT_COMMITTER_NAME='DhanushPrince' GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL='r.dhanush307@gmail.com' \
     git commit-tree "$TREE" -p "$PARENT")
   git reset --hard "$NEW"
   ```
3. Only then `git push`.

## User setting (remind once if trailer keeps coming back)

Cursor Settings → **Agents / Git & PRs → Attribution** → turn **off** commit and PR attribution.
